{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"language":"python","display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12.13","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":16903622}],"dockerImageVersionId":31400,"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":true}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"source":"<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/trmtkb/trmtkb-sentiment-eda?scriptVersionId=327928600\" target=\"_blank\"><img align=\"left\" alt=\"Kaggle\" title=\"Open in Kaggle\" src=\"https://kaggle.com/static/images/open-in-kaggle.svg\"></a>","metadata":{},"cell_type":"markdown"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Tonbokiri Creative Writing with AI: GoEmotions Analysis\nA home-crafted GoEmotions analysis notebook for original Japanese AI-assisted fiction. Built with Gemma 2B and refined with an Arena.ai agent, it turns dialogue sessions into radar charts, pie charts, and stacked emotion bars.\n\nA home-brewed emotion atlas for original Japanese AI-assisted fiction, refined with an Arena.ai agent.\n\n## Overview\nA Kaggle notebook for emotion analysis of custom creative-writing dialogue sessions.\nThis notebook uses **Gemma 2B Japanese Instruct** to assign **GoEmotions** labels\nand visualize emotional patterns across the **user**, **AI1**, and **AI2**.\n\n- **Dataset:** custom JSON dialogue sessions\n- **Model:** `google/gemma-2-2b-jpn-it`\n- **Emotion schema:** GoEmotions (28 labels)\n- **Outputs:** CSV summaries, radar charts, pie charts, and stacked bar charts\n\n### Sections\n### 1. Setup\nInstall dependencies and define notebook settings.\n\n### 2. Emotion inference with Gemma\nLoad the model, parse JSON sessions, and infer GoEmotions labels.\n\n### 3. CSV outputs\nSave detailed and summarized results for fast re-plotting.\n\n**  4. Radar and pie charts **\nQuick visual overview of role-based emotion distributions.\n\n### 5. Stacked bar charts by emotion\nCompare **role share inside each emotion**.\n\n### 6. Alternative stacked bar charts by role\nCompare **emotion composition inside each role**.\n\n### Notes\n- `MAX_SAMPLES_PER_WORK = 100`\n- `TOP_N_EMOTIONS = 15`\n- Re-running visualization cells does **not** require re-running Gemma inference if the CSVs already exist.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 1. Setup\nInstall dependencies and define notebook settings.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ============================================================\n# Kaggle Notebook 完成版 v4\n# Tonbokiri Creative Writing with AI: GoEmotions Analysis\n#\n# 反映内容\n# - conditional install\n# - MAX_SAMPLES_PER_WORK = 100\n# - CELL 6 最終版（X_LABEL_SIZE=20, ROTATION=58, TITLE_SIZE=28）\n# - CELL 7 発表向け配色版（感情ごとの固定色）\n# - Markdown / TOC 向けの見出し例つき\n# ============================================================","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-17T18:35:47.885001Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-17T18:35:47.885711Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-17T18:35:47.889822Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-17T18:35:47.88568Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-17T18:35:47.889083Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==================== CELL 0: Markdown（任意） ====================\n# # Tonbokiri Creative Writing with AI: GoEmotions Analysis\n#\n# A Kaggle notebook for emotion analysis of custom creative-writing dialogue sessions.\n# This notebook uses **Gemma 2B Japanese Instruct** to assign **GoEmotions** labels\n# and visualize emotional patterns across the **user**, **AI1**, and **AI2**.\n#\n# ## Overview\n# - **Dataset:** custom JSON dialogue sessions\n# - **Model:** `google/gemma-2-2b-jpn-it`\n# - **Emotion schema:** GoEmotions (28 labels)\n# - **Outputs:** CSV summaries, radar charts, pie charts, and stacked bar charts\n#\n# ## 1. Setup\n# ## 2. Load model and infer emotions\n# ## 3. Save CSV outputs\n# ## 4. Radar and pie charts\n# ## 5. Stacked bars by emotion\n# ## 6. Alternative stacked bars by role\n# ## 7. Quick tuning notes\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-17T21:11:14.670147Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-17T21:11:14.670938Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-17T21:11:14.67424Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-17T21:11:14.670904Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-17T21:11:14.673403Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==================== CELL 1: conditional install ====================\nimport importlib.util\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\n\nrequired = [\n    (\"transformers\", \"transformers\"),\n    (\"accelerate\", \"accelerate\"),\n    (\"sentencepiece\", \"sentencepiece\"),\n]\n\nmissing = [pip_name for module_name, pip_name in required if importlib.util.find_spec(module_name) is None]\n\nif missing:\n    print(\"Installing:\", \", \".join(missing))\n    subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"-q\", *missing])\nelse:\n    print(\"All required packages are already available. Skipping pip install.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-17T18:35:47.904539Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-17T18:35:47.904887Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-17T18:35:47.918755Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-17T18:35:47.904826Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-17T18:35:47.918117Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==================== CELL 2: imports & config ====================\nimport os\nimport re\nimport json\nfrom typing import List, Dict\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport matplotlib.ticker as mtick\nimport torch\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForCausalLM\n\nplt.rcParams[\"figure.facecolor\"] = \"white\"\nplt.rcParams[\"axes.grid\"] = True\nplt.rcParams[\"grid.alpha\"] = 0.25\nplt.rcParams[\"figure.dpi\"] = 140\nplt.rcParams[\"savefig.dpi\"] = 180\n\nMODEL_NAME = \"google/gemma-2-2b-jpn-it\"\nMAX_SAMPLES_PER_WORK = 100\nBATCH_SIZE = 4\nMAX_INPUT_CHARS = 700\nMAX_NEW_TOKENS = 12\n\nDETAIL_CSV = \"/kaggle/working/sentiment_gemma_goemotions.csv\"\nSUMMARY_CSV = \"/kaggle/working/sentiment_gemma_summary.csv\"\n\nGOEMOTIONS_LABELS = [\n    \"admiration\", \"amusement\", \"anger\", \"annoyance\", \"approval\", \"caring\", \"confusion\",\n    \"curiosity\", \"desire\", \"disappointment\", \"disapproval\", \"disgust\", \"embarrassment\",\n    \"excitement\", \"fear\", \"gratitude\", \"grief\", \"joy\", \"love\", \"nervous\", \"optimism\",\n    \"pride\", \"realization\", \"relief\", \"remorse\", \"sadness\", \"surprise\", \"neutral\"\n]\n\nPRIMARY_EMOTIONS = [\n    \"joy\", \"sadness\", \"anger\", \"fear\", \"surprise\",\n    \"disgust\", \"neutral\", \"excitement\", \"love\", \"admiration\"\n]\n\nROLE_ORDER = [\"user\", \"assistant_a\", \"assistant_b\", \"unknown\"]\nROLE_LABELS = {\n    \"user\": \"user\",\n    \"assistant_a\": \"AI1\",\n    \"assistant_b\": \"AI2\",\n    \"unknown\": \"unknown\",\n}\nROLE_COLORS = {\n    \"user\": \"#2196F3\",\n    \"assistant_a\": \"#FF9800\",\n    \"assistant_b\": \"#9C27B0\",\n    \"unknown\": \"#9E9E9E\",\n}\n\n# 発表向け: 感情ごとの色\nEMOTION_COLORS = {\n    # admiration を主役に\n    \"admiration\": \"#FF4FA3\",\n    \"love\": \"#FF7EB6\",\n    \"gratitude\": \"#FFB347\",\n    \"approval\": \"#FF8C69\",\n    \"caring\": \"#F497B6\",\n    \"optimism\": \"#FFA94D\",\n    \"pride\": \"#D96CFF\",\n    \"relief\": \"#FFD166\",\n    \"desire\": \"#F78FB3\",\n\n    # laugh / bright\n    \"joy\": \"#FFD93D\",\n    \"amusement\": \"#FFC300\",\n    \"excitement\": \"#FF9F1C\",\n\n    # sad / cold\n    \"sadness\": \"#4D96FF\",\n    \"grief\": \"#355CDE\",\n    \"remorse\": \"#6C8AE4\",\n    \"disappointment\": \"#6FA8DC\",\n    \"fear\": \"#5B7CFA\",\n\n    # question / gray\n    \"confusion\": \"#7A7A7A\",\n    \"neutral\": \"#BDBDBD\",\n    \"nervous\": \"#8D99AE\",\n    \"realization\": \"#95A5A6\",\n    \"embarrassment\": \"#A1887F\",\n\n    # rare / green\n    \"curiosity\": \"#2ECC71\",\n    \"surprise\": \"#20C997\",\n\n    # strong negative\n    \"anger\": \"#E63946\",\n    \"annoyance\": \"#C44536\",\n    \"disapproval\": \"#8E44AD\",\n    \"disgust\": \"#2E8B57\",\n}\n\nprint(\"Config loaded.\")\nprint(f\"MODEL_NAME={MODEL_NAME}\")\nprint(f\"MAX_SAMPLES_PER_WORK={MAX_SAMPLES_PER_WORK}\")\nprint(f\"BATCH_SIZE={BATCH_SIZE}\")\nprint(f\"MAX_NEW_TOKENS={MAX_NEW_TOKENS}\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-17T18:35:47.91987Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-17T18:35:47.920144Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-17T18:35:54.930878Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-17T18:35:47.920115Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-17T18:35:54.929989Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 2. Load model and infer emotions\nLoad Gemma, parse JSON dialogue sessions, and infer GoEmotions labels.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\n# ==================== CELL 3: helper functions ====================\ndef normalize_text(text: str) -> str:\n    text = str(text).replace(\"\\r\", \" \").replace(\"\\n\", \" \")\n    text = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", text).strip()\n    return text[:MAX_INPUT_CHARS]\n\n\ndef unify_role(msg: Dict) -> str:\n    candidates = [\n        msg.get(\"speaker\", \"\"),\n        msg.get(\"name\", \"\"),\n        msg.get(\"model\", \"\"),\n        msg.get(\"role\", \"\"),\n        msg.get(\"author\", \"\"),\n    ]\n    joined = \" | \".join([str(x).lower().strip() for x in candidates if x is not None])\n\n    if \"user\" in joined or \"作者\" in joined:\n        return \"user\"\n    if \"assistant_a\" in joined or \"assistant a\" in joined or re.search(r\"(^|\\W)a(\\W|$)\", joined):\n        return \"assistant_a\"\n    if \"assistant_b\" in joined or \"assistant b\" in joined or re.search(r\"(^|\\W)b(\\W|$)\", joined):\n        return \"assistant_b\"\n    return \"unknown\"\n\n\ndef extract_content(msg: Dict) -> str:\n    for key in [\"content\", \"text\", \"body\", \"message\", \"value\"]:\n        value = msg.get(key, \"\")\n        if value and str(value).strip():\n            return str(value)\n    return \"\"\n\n\ndef load_session_json(json_path: str) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    with open(json_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        data = json.load(f)\n\n    if isinstance(data, list):\n        messages = data\n    elif isinstance(data, dict):\n        if isinstance(data.get(\"turns\"), list):\n            messages = data[\"turns\"]\n        elif isinstance(data.get(\"messages\"), list):\n            messages = data[\"messages\"]\n        elif isinstance(data.get(\"conversation\"), list):\n            messages = data[\"conversation\"]\n        else:\n            return pd.DataFrame()\n    else:\n        return pd.DataFrame()\n\n    rows = []\n    for msg in messages:\n        if not isinstance(msg, dict):\n            continue\n\n        content = extract_content(msg)\n        if not content.strip():\n            continue\n\n        rows.append({\n            \"role_unified\": unify_role(msg),\n            \"speaker\": str(msg.get(\"speaker\", msg.get(\"name\", msg.get(\"model\", msg.get(\"role\", \"\"))))),\n            \"content\": content,\n        })\n\n    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n\n\ndef build_prompt(text: str) -> str:\n    clean = normalize_text(text)\n    labels_text = \", \".join(GOEMOTIONS_LABELS)\n    return f\"\"\"あなたは感情分析器です。\n次の文章の感情を、GoEmotionsラベル一覧から1〜3個選んでください。\n該当が弱い場合は neutral を選んでください。\n\n重要:\n- 返答はラベル名だけ\n- 半角カンマ区切り\n- 説明文・理由・見出し・記号は禁止\n- 使ってよいラベルは一覧の中だけ\n\nラベル一覧:\n{labels_text}\n\n文章:\n{clean}\n\n回答:\"\"\"\n\n\ndef parse_emotions(output_text: str) -> List[str]:\n    if not output_text:\n        return [\"neutral\"]\n\n    text = str(output_text).lower().strip().replace(\"**\", \" \")\n\n    for stop_word in [\"explanation\", \"理由\", \"説明\", \"note:\", \"answer:\"]:\n        if stop_word in text:\n            text = text.split(stop_word)[0]\n\n    lines = [ln.strip() for ln in text.splitlines() if ln.strip()]\n    head = \" \".join(lines[:2]) if lines else text\n\n    parts = re.split(r\"[,/;\\n]+\", head)\n    labels = []\n    for p in parts:\n        p = re.sub(r\"[^a-z_]\", \"\", p.strip())\n        if p in GOEMOTIONS_LABELS and p not in labels:\n            labels.append(p)\n\n    if not labels:\n        for lbl in GOEMOTIONS_LABELS:\n            if re.search(rf\"\\b{re.escape(lbl)}\\b\", head):\n                labels.append(lbl)\n\n    return labels if labels else [\"neutral\"]\n\n\ndef load_hf_token():\n    try:\n        from kaggle_secrets import UserSecretsClient\n        user_secrets = UserSecretsClient()\n        hf_token = user_secrets.get_secret(\"HF_TOKEN\")\n        os.environ[\"HF_TOKEN\"] = hf_token\n        print(\"HF_TOKEN loaded from Kaggle Secrets.\")\n        return hf_token\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Warning: {e}\")\n        return os.environ.get(\"HF_TOKEN\", None)\n\n\ndef choose_dtype():\n    return torch.float16 if torch.cuda.is_available() else torch.float32\n\n\ndef load_model_and_tokenizer(model_name: str, hf_token: str = None):\n    print(f\"Loading Gemma: {model_name}\")\n    tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name, token=hf_token)\n    if tokenizer.pad_token_id is None:\n        tokenizer.pad_token = tokenizer.eos_token\n    tokenizer.padding_side = \"left\"\n\n    model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\n        model_name,\n        token=hf_token,\n        dtype=choose_dtype(),\n        device_map=\"auto\",\n    )\n    model.eval()\n\n    model.generation_config.pad_token_id = tokenizer.pad_token_id\n    model.generation_config.eos_token_id = tokenizer.eos_token_id\n    try:\n        model.generation_config.max_length = None\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n    return tokenizer, model\n\n\ndef generate_batch(prompts: List[str], tokenizer, model) -> List[str]:\n    if not prompts:\n        return []\n\n    input_device = next(model.parameters()).device\n    encoded = tokenizer(\n        prompts,\n        return_tensors=\"pt\",\n        padding=True,\n        truncation=True,\n        max_length=1024,\n    )\n    encoded = {k: v.to(input_device) for k, v in encoded.items()}\n\n    with torch.inference_mode():\n        outputs = model.generate(\n            **encoded,\n            max_new_tokens=MAX_NEW_TOKENS,\n            do_sample=False,\n            pad_token_id=tokenizer.pad_token_id,\n            eos_token_id=tokenizer.eos_token_id,\n            use_cache=True,\n        )\n\n    prompt_len = encoded[\"input_ids\"].shape[1]\n    generated_only = outputs[:, prompt_len:]\n    texts = tokenizer.batch_decode(generated_only, skip_special_tokens=True)\n    return texts\n\n\ndef infer_emotions_for_df(df: pd.DataFrame, work_name: str, tokenizer, model) -> List[Dict]:\n    records = []\n    texts = df[\"content\"].astype(str).tolist()\n    roles = df[\"role_unified\"].astype(str).tolist()\n    prompts = [build_prompt(t) for t in texts]\n\n    total = len(prompts)\n    for start in range(0, total, BATCH_SIZE):\n        end = min(start + BATCH_SIZE, total)\n        batch_prompts = prompts[start:end]\n        batch_roles = roles[start:end]\n\n        try:\n            batch_outputs = generate_batch(batch_prompts, tokenizer, model)\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"    → バッチ推論エラー ({start}:{end}): {e}\")\n            batch_outputs = [\"neutral\"] * len(batch_prompts)\n\n        for role, raw_output in zip(batch_roles, batch_outputs):\n            labels = parse_emotions(raw_output)\n            for lbl in labels:\n                records.append({\n                    \"work\": work_name,\n                    \"role_unified\": role,\n                    \"label\": lbl,\n                    \"raw_output\": str(raw_output)[:120],\n                })\n\n        print(f\"    - batch {start + 1:>3}-{end:<3} / {total}\")\n\n    return records\n\nprint(\"Helpers loaded.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-17T18:35:54.932686Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-17T18:35:54.933159Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-17T18:35:54.957902Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-17T18:35:54.93313Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-17T18:35:54.956947Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 3. Save CSV outputs\nSave detailed and summarized outputs for fast re-plotting.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==================== CELL 4: inference & save CSV ====================\nhf_token = load_hf_token()\ntokenizer, model = load_model_and_tokenizer(MODEL_NAME, hf_token)\n\njson_files = []\nfor root, _, files in os.walk(\"/kaggle/input/\"):\n    for f in files:\n        if f.endswith(\".json\") and not f.startswith(\"kernel-metadata\") and not f.startswith(\"dataset-metadata\"):\n            json_files.append(os.path.join(root, f))\n\njson_files = sorted(json_files)\nprint(f\"Found {len(json_files)} JSON files\")\n\nall_results = []\nfor json_path in json_files:\n    work_name = os.path.basename(json_path).replace(\".json\", \"\")\n    print(f\"\\n[Analyzing] {work_name} ...\")\n\n    df = load_session_json(json_path)\n    if df.empty:\n        print(\"  -> skip (no valid rows)\")\n        continue\n\n    if MAX_SAMPLES_PER_WORK is not None and len(df) > MAX_SAMPLES_PER_WORK:\n        df = df.head(MAX_SAMPLES_PER_WORK)\n\n    print(f\"  -> processing {len(df)} rows\")\n    work_results = infer_emotions_for_df(df, work_name, tokenizer, model)\n    all_results.extend(work_results)\n    print(f\"  -> cumulative labels: {len(all_results)}\")\n\ncombined = pd.DataFrame(all_results)\nprint(f\"\\nTotal labels: {len(combined)}\")\n\nif combined.empty:\n    raise SystemExit(\"ERROR: no valid data was produced.\")\n\nsummary = combined.groupby([\"work\", \"role_unified\", \"label\"]).size().reset_index(name=\"count\")\ntotals = combined.groupby([\"work\", \"role_unified\"]).size().reset_index(name=\"total\")\nsummary = summary.merge(totals, on=[\"work\", \"role_unified\"], how=\"left\")\nsummary[\"ratio\"] = summary[\"count\"] / summary[\"total\"]\n\ncombined.to_csv(DETAIL_CSV, index=False, encoding=\"utf-8-sig\")\nsummary.to_csv(SUMMARY_CSV, index=False, encoding=\"utf-8-sig\")\n\nprint(f\"Saved: {DETAIL_CSV}\")\nprint(f\"Saved: {SUMMARY_CSV}\")\nprint(summary.sort_values(\"count\", ascending=False).head(20))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-17T18:35:54.958825Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-17T18:35:54.959079Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-17T18:37:27.788402Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-17T18:35:54.959056Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-17T18:37:27.787535Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 4. Radar and pie charts\nA quick visual overview of role-based emotional distributions.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==================== CELL 5: radar + pie ====================\nsummary = pd.read_csv(SUMMARY_CSV)\n\npivot_data = summary[summary[\"label\"].isin(PRIMARY_EMOTIONS)].pivot_table(\n    index=[\"work\", \"role_unified\"],\n    columns=\"label\",\n    values=\"ratio\",\n    fill_value=0,\n).reset_index()\n\nworks = pivot_data[\"work\"].unique().tolist()\nangles = np.linspace(0, 2 * np.pi, len(PRIMARY_EMOTIONS), endpoint=False).tolist()\nangles += angles[:1]\n\ncols = 3\nrows = (len(works) + cols - 1) // cols\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(rows, cols, figsize=(cols * 6, rows * 6), subplot_kw=dict(polar=True))\naxes = np.array(axes).reshape(-1)\n\nfor idx, work in enumerate(works):\n    ax = axes[idx]\n    sub = pivot_data[pivot_data[\"work\"] == work]\n\n    for role in ROLE_ORDER:\n        role_data = sub[sub[\"role_unified\"] == role]\n        if role_data.empty:\n            continue\n\n        values = [role_data[emo].values[0] if emo in role_data.columns else 0 for emo in PRIMARY_EMOTIONS]\n        values += values[:1]\n        ax.plot(angles, values, \"o-\", linewidth=2, label=ROLE_LABELS.get(role, role), color=ROLE_COLORS.get(role, \"#999999\"))\n        ax.fill(angles, values, alpha=0.12, color=ROLE_COLORS.get(role, \"#999999\"))\n\n    ax.set_xticks(angles[:-1])\n    ax.set_xticklabels(PRIMARY_EMOTIONS, fontsize=9)\n    ax.set_ylim(0, 1)\n    ax.set_title(work, fontsize=11, pad=15)\n\n    handles, labels = ax.get_legend_handles_labels()\n    if handles:\n        ax.legend(loc=\"upper right\", bbox_to_anchor=(1.3, 1.1), fontsize=8)\n\nfor idx in range(len(works), len(axes)):\n    axes[idx].axis(\"off\")\n\nplt.suptitle(\"GoEmotions Primary Emotions Radar (Gemma 2B)\", fontsize=14, y=1.02)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n\nif len(works) > 0:\n    target_work = works[0]\n    full_pivot = summary.pivot_table(\n        index=[\"work\", \"role_unified\"],\n        columns=\"label\",\n        values=\"ratio\",\n        fill_value=0,\n    ).reset_index()\n\n    sub = full_pivot[full_pivot[\"work\"] == target_work]\n    all_labels = sorted([c for c in full_pivot.columns if c not in (\"work\", \"role_unified\")])\n    angles_full = np.linspace(0, 2 * np.pi, len(all_labels), endpoint=False).tolist()\n    angles_full += angles_full[:1]\n\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 10), subplot_kw=dict(polar=True))\n\n    for role in ROLE_ORDER:\n        role_data = sub[sub[\"role_unified\"] == role]\n        if role_data.empty:\n            continue\n\n        values = [role_data[lbl].values[0] if lbl in role_data.columns else 0 for lbl in all_labels]\n        values += values[:1]\n        ax.plot(angles_full, values, \"o-\", linewidth=1.5, label=ROLE_LABELS.get(role, role), color=ROLE_COLORS.get(role, \"#999999\"), alpha=0.85)\n        ax.fill(angles_full, values, alpha=0.08, color=ROLE_COLORS.get(role, \"#999999\"))\n\n    ax.set_xticks(angles_full[:-1])\n    ax.set_xticklabels(all_labels, fontsize=7, rotation=45)\n    ax.set_ylim(0, 1)\n    ax.set_title(f\"{target_work} - Full GoEmotions Radar (28 labels)\", fontsize=12, pad=15)\n    handles, labels = ax.get_legend_handles_labels()\n    if handles:\n        ax.legend(loc=\"upper right\", bbox_to_anchor=(1.3, 1.1))\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.show()\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(rows, cols, figsize=(cols * 5, rows * 5))\naxes = np.array(axes).reshape(-1)\n\nfor idx, work in enumerate(works):\n    ax = axes[idx]\n    sub = summary[summary[\"work\"] == work]\n    if sub.empty:\n        ax.axis(\"off\")\n        continue\n\n    pie_data = sub.groupby(\"role_unified\")[\"ratio\"].mean().sort_values(ascending=False)\n    colors = [ROLE_COLORS.get(role, \"#999999\") for role in pie_data.index]\n    labels = [ROLE_LABELS.get(role, role) for role in pie_data.index]\n    ax.pie(pie_data.values, labels=labels, autopct=\"%1.1f%%\", colors=colors, startangle=90)\n    ax.set_title(f\"{work}\\n(Avg Sentiment Share)\")\n\nfor idx in range(len(works), len(axes)):\n    axes[idx].axis(\"off\")\n\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-17T18:37:27.789414Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-17T18:37:27.78968Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-17T18:37:30.582221Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-17T18:37:27.789657Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-17T18:37:30.581325Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 5. Stacked bars by emotion\nEmotion-first stacked bar views for comparing how each emotion is distributed across the user, AI1, and AI2.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"#I like it :D","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### 5.1 Role-color version\nA role-first color design: **user**, **AI1**, and **AI2** are distinguished by color.\nThis version is the most direct and easy to read for structural comparison.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==================== CELL 6: stacked bars by emotion (FINAL) ====================\nsummary = pd.read_csv(SUMMARY_CSV)\n\nWORKS_PER_FIG = 2\nTOP_N_EMOTIONS = 15\nPLOT_ZERO_EMOTIONS = False\nSORT_MODE = \"count\"\nFIG_WIDTH = 24\nROW_HEIGHT = 11.5\nROTATION = 58\nBAR_WIDTH = 0.82\nX_LABEL_SIZE = 20\nY_TICK_SIZE = 13\nTITLE_SIZE = 28\nAXIS_LABEL_SIZE = 16\nLEGEND_SIZE = 14\nSUPTITLE_SIZE = 20\n\nprint(f\"WORKS_PER_FIG={WORKS_PER_FIG}\")\nprint(f\"TOP_N_EMOTIONS={TOP_N_EMOTIONS}\")\nprint(f\"PLOT_ZERO_EMOTIONS={PLOT_ZERO_EMOTIONS}\")\nprint(f\"SORT_MODE={SORT_MODE}\")\n\n\ndef prepare_work_tables(summary_df, work_name):\n    sub = summary_df[summary_df[\"work\"] == work_name].copy()\n    if sub.empty:\n        return None, None\n\n    count_table = sub.pivot_table(\n        index=\"label\",\n        columns=\"role_unified\",\n        values=\"count\",\n        aggfunc=\"sum\",\n        fill_value=0,\n    )\n\n    for role in ROLE_ORDER:\n        if role not in count_table.columns:\n            count_table[role] = 0\n\n    count_table = count_table[ROLE_ORDER]\n\n    if PLOT_ZERO_EMOTIONS:\n        count_table = count_table.reindex(GOEMOTIONS_LABELS, fill_value=0)\n    else:\n        count_table = count_table[count_table.sum(axis=1) > 0]\n\n    if count_table.empty:\n        return None, None\n\n    count_table[\"_sum_\"] = count_table.sum(axis=1)\n\n    if SORT_MODE == \"label\":\n        ordered_labels = [lbl for lbl in GOEMOTIONS_LABELS if lbl in count_table.index]\n        count_table = count_table.loc[ordered_labels]\n    else:\n        count_table = count_table.sort_values(\"_sum_\", ascending=False)\n\n    if TOP_N_EMOTIONS is not None:\n        count_table = count_table.head(TOP_N_EMOTIONS)\n\n    totals = count_table[\"_sum_\"].copy()\n    count_table = count_table.drop(columns=[\"_sum_\"])\n    pct_table = count_table.div(totals, axis=0) * 100\n\n    return count_table, pct_table\n\n\ndef plot_one_work_pair(ax_pct, ax_cnt, work_name, count_table, pct_table):\n    labels = count_table.index.tolist()\n    x = np.arange(len(labels))\n\n    bottom_pct = np.zeros(len(labels))\n    bottom_cnt = np.zeros(len(labels))\n\n    for role in ROLE_ORDER:\n        pct_vals = pct_table[role].values if role in pct_table.columns else np.zeros(len(labels))\n        cnt_vals = count_table[role].values if role in count_table.columns else np.zeros(len(labels))\n\n        if np.sum(pct_vals) == 0 and np.sum(cnt_vals) == 0:\n            continue\n\n        ax_pct.bar(\n            x, pct_vals, bottom=bottom_pct, width=BAR_WIDTH,\n            color=ROLE_COLORS.get(role, \"#999999\"), label=ROLE_LABELS.get(role, role)\n        )\n        ax_cnt.bar(\n            x, cnt_vals, bottom=bottom_cnt, width=BAR_WIDTH,\n            color=ROLE_COLORS.get(role, \"#999999\"), label=ROLE_LABELS.get(role, role)\n        )\n\n        bottom_pct += pct_vals\n        bottom_cnt += cnt_vals\n\n    ax_pct.set_title(f\"{work_name} | 100% stacked by emotion\", fontsize=TITLE_SIZE)\n    ax_pct.set_xticks(x)\n    ax_pct.set_xticklabels(\n        labels,\n        rotation=ROTATION,\n        ha=\"right\",\n        fontsize=X_LABEL_SIZE,\n        fontstyle=\"italic\",\n    )\n    ax_pct.set_ylabel(\"%\", fontsize=AXIS_LABEL_SIZE)\n    ax_pct.set_ylim(0, 100)\n    ax_pct.yaxis.set_major_formatter(mtick.PercentFormatter())\n    ax_pct.grid(axis=\"y\", alpha=0.3)\n    ax_pct.tick_params(axis=\"x\", pad=10)\n    ax_pct.tick_params(axis=\"y\", labelsize=Y_TICK_SIZE)\n\n    ax_cnt.set_title(f\"{work_name} | stacked counts by emotion\", fontsize=TITLE_SIZE)\n    ax_cnt.set_xticks(x)\n    ax_cnt.set_xticklabels(\n        labels,\n        rotation=ROTATION,\n        ha=\"right\",\n        fontsize=X_LABEL_SIZE,\n        fontstyle=\"italic\",\n    )\n    ax_cnt.set_ylabel(\"count\", fontsize=AXIS_LABEL_SIZE)\n    ax_cnt.grid(axis=\"y\", alpha=0.3)\n    ax_cnt.tick_params(axis=\"x\", pad=10)\n    ax_cnt.tick_params(axis=\"y\", labelsize=Y_TICK_SIZE)\n\n\nworks = summary[\"work\"].dropna().unique().tolist()\nprint(f\"Works: {len(works)}\")\n\nfor start in range(0, len(works), WORKS_PER_FIG):\n    chunk = works[start:start + WORKS_PER_FIG]\n    nrows = len(chunk)\n\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(\n        nrows=nrows,\n        ncols=2,\n        figsize=(FIG_WIDTH, ROW_HEIGHT * nrows),\n        constrained_layout=True,\n    )\n\n    if nrows == 1:\n        axes = np.array([axes])\n\n    legend_handles = None\n    legend_labels = None\n\n    for row_idx, work_name in enumerate(chunk):\n        ax_pct = axes[row_idx, 0]\n        ax_cnt = axes[row_idx, 1]\n\n        count_table, pct_table = prepare_work_tables(summary, work_name)\n        if count_table is None or pct_table is None or count_table.empty:\n            ax_pct.axis(\"off\")\n            ax_cnt.axis(\"off\")\n            continue\n\n        plot_one_work_pair(ax_pct, ax_cnt, work_name, count_table, pct_table)\n\n        if legend_handles is None:\n            legend_handles, legend_labels = ax_pct.get_legend_handles_labels()\n\n    if legend_handles:\n        fig.legend(\n            legend_handles,\n            legend_labels,\n            loc=\"upper center\",\n            ncol=min(len(legend_labels), 4),\n            bbox_to_anchor=(0.5, 1.02),\n            frameon=True,\n            fontsize=LEGEND_SIZE,\n        )\n\n    fig.suptitle(\n        f\"GoEmotions Stacked Bar Charts ({start + 1}-{start + len(chunk)} Opus)\",\n        fontsize=SUPTITLE_SIZE,\n        y=1.03,\n    )\n    plt.show()\n\nprint(\"=== stacked bar by emotion done ===\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-17T21:12:22.853519Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-17T21:12:22.854152Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-17T21:12:27.155325Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-17T21:12:22.854122Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-17T21:12:27.154466Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### 5.2 Emotion-palette version\nAn emotion-first color design using a custom GoEmotions palette.\nThis version emphasizes the emotional atmosphere of each work while retaining role differences through patterns.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==================== CELL 6B: stacked bars by emotion (emotion palette variant) ====================\n# 目的:\n# - CELL 7 と同じ EMOTION_COLORS を使う\n# - x軸は感情のまま\n# - bar のベース色 = 感情色\n# - user / AI1 / AI2 の違いは hatch (模様) で表現\n#\n# 前提:\n# - CELL 2 が実行済み\n# - SUMMARY_CSV, GOEMOTIONS_LABELS, ROLE_ORDER, ROLE_LABELS, EMOTION_COLORS が定義済み\n\nfrom matplotlib.patches import Patch\n\nsummary = pd.read_csv(SUMMARY_CSV)\n\nWORKS_PER_FIG = 2\nTOP_N_EMOTIONS = 15\nPLOT_ZERO_EMOTIONS = False\nSORT_MODE = \"count\"\nFIG_WIDTH = 24\nROW_HEIGHT = 11.8\nROTATION = 58\nBAR_WIDTH = 0.82\nX_LABEL_SIZE = 20\nY_TICK_SIZE = 13\nTITLE_SIZE = 28\nAXIS_LABEL_SIZE = 16\nLEGEND_SIZE = 14\nSUPTITLE_SIZE = 20\nEDGE_COLOR = \"#444444\"\nLINE_WIDTH = 1.0\n\nROLE_HATCHES = {\n    \"user\": \"\",\n    \"assistant_a\": \"x\",\n    \"assistant_b\": \"/\",\n    \"unknown\": \"-x\",\n}\n\nprint(f\"WORKS_PER_FIG={WORKS_PER_FIG}\")\nprint(f\"TOP_N_EMOTIONS={TOP_N_EMOTIONS}\")\nprint(f\"PLOT_ZERO_EMOTIONS={PLOT_ZERO_EMOTIONS}\")\nprint(f\"SORT_MODE={SORT_MODE}\")\n\n\ndef prepare_work_tables(summary_df, work_name):\n    sub = summary_df[summary_df[\"work\"] == work_name].copy()\n    if sub.empty:\n        return None, None\n\n    count_table = sub.pivot_table(\n        index=\"label\",\n        columns=\"role_unified\",\n        values=\"count\",\n        aggfunc=\"sum\",\n        fill_value=0,\n    )\n\n    for role in ROLE_ORDER:\n        if role not in count_table.columns:\n            count_table[role] = 0\n\n    count_table = count_table[ROLE_ORDER]\n\n    if PLOT_ZERO_EMOTIONS:\n        count_table = count_table.reindex(GOEMOTIONS_LABELS, fill_value=0)\n    else:\n        count_table = count_table[count_table.sum(axis=1) > 0]\n\n    if count_table.empty:\n        return None, None\n\n    count_table[\"_sum_\"] = count_table.sum(axis=1)\n\n    if SORT_MODE == \"label\":\n        ordered_labels = [lbl for lbl in GOEMOTIONS_LABELS if lbl in count_table.index]\n        count_table = count_table.loc[ordered_labels]\n    else:\n        count_table = count_table.sort_values(\"_sum_\", ascending=False)\n\n    if TOP_N_EMOTIONS is not None:\n        count_table = count_table.head(TOP_N_EMOTIONS)\n\n    totals = count_table[\"_sum_\"].copy()\n    count_table = count_table.drop(columns=[\"_sum_\"])\n    pct_table = count_table.div(totals, axis=0) * 100\n\n    return count_table, pct_table\n\n\ndef plot_one_work_pair(ax_pct, ax_cnt, work_name, count_table, pct_table):\n    labels = count_table.index.tolist()\n    x = np.arange(len(labels))\n\n    bottom_pct = np.zeros(len(labels))\n    bottom_cnt = np.zeros(len(labels))\n\n    for role in ROLE_ORDER:\n        pct_vals = pct_table[role].values if role in pct_table.columns else np.zeros(len(labels))\n        cnt_vals = count_table[role].values if role in count_table.columns else np.zeros(len(labels))\n\n        if np.sum(pct_vals) == 0 and np.sum(cnt_vals) == 0:\n            continue\n\n        colors = [EMOTION_COLORS.get(lbl, \"#BBBBBB\") for lbl in labels]\n        hatch = ROLE_HATCHES.get(role, \"\")\n\n        ax_pct.bar(\n            x,\n            pct_vals,\n            bottom=bottom_pct,\n            width=BAR_WIDTH,\n            color=colors,\n            hatch=hatch,\n            edgecolor=EDGE_COLOR,\n            linewidth=LINE_WIDTH,\n            label=ROLE_LABELS.get(role, role),\n        )\n        ax_cnt.bar(\n            x,\n            cnt_vals,\n            bottom=bottom_cnt,\n            width=BAR_WIDTH,\n            color=colors,\n            hatch=hatch,\n            edgecolor=EDGE_COLOR,\n            linewidth=LINE_WIDTH,\n            label=ROLE_LABELS.get(role, role),\n        )\n\n        bottom_pct += pct_vals\n        bottom_cnt += cnt_vals\n\n    ax_pct.set_title(f\"{work_name} | 100% stacked by emotion\", fontsize=TITLE_SIZE)\n    ax_pct.set_xticks(x)\n    ax_pct.set_xticklabels(\n        labels,\n        rotation=ROTATION,\n        ha=\"right\",\n        fontsize=X_LABEL_SIZE,\n        fontstyle=\"italic\",\n    )\n    ax_pct.set_ylabel(\"%\", fontsize=AXIS_LABEL_SIZE)\n    ax_pct.set_ylim(0, 100)\n    ax_pct.yaxis.set_major_formatter(mtick.PercentFormatter())\n    ax_pct.grid(axis=\"y\", alpha=0.3)\n    ax_pct.tick_params(axis=\"x\", pad=10)\n    ax_pct.tick_params(axis=\"y\", labelsize=Y_TICK_SIZE)\n\n    ax_cnt.set_title(f\"{work_name} | stacked counts by emotion\", fontsize=TITLE_SIZE)\n    ax_cnt.set_xticks(x)\n    ax_cnt.set_xticklabels(\n        labels,\n        rotation=ROTATION,\n        ha=\"right\",\n        fontsize=X_LABEL_SIZE,\n        fontstyle=\"italic\",\n    )\n    ax_cnt.set_ylabel(\"count\", fontsize=AXIS_LABEL_SIZE)\n    ax_cnt.grid(axis=\"y\", alpha=0.3)\n    ax_cnt.tick_params(axis=\"x\", pad=10)\n    ax_cnt.tick_params(axis=\"y\", labelsize=Y_TICK_SIZE)\n\n\nworks = summary[\"work\"].dropna().unique().tolist()\nprint(f\"Works: {len(works)}\")\n\nfor start in range(0, len(works), WORKS_PER_FIG):\n    chunk = works[start:start + WORKS_PER_FIG]\n    nrows = len(chunk)\n\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(\n        nrows=nrows,\n        ncols=2,\n        figsize=(FIG_WIDTH, ROW_HEIGHT * nrows),\n        constrained_layout=True,\n    )\n\n    if nrows == 1:\n        axes = np.array([axes])\n\n    for row_idx, work_name in enumerate(chunk):\n        ax_pct = axes[row_idx, 0]\n        ax_cnt = axes[row_idx, 1]\n\n        count_table, pct_table = prepare_work_tables(summary, work_name)\n        if count_table is None or pct_table is None or count_table.empty:\n            ax_pct.axis(\"off\")\n            ax_cnt.axis(\"off\")\n            continue\n\n        plot_one_work_pair(ax_pct, ax_cnt, work_name, count_table, pct_table)\n\n    role_legend_handles = [\n        Patch(\n            facecolor=\"white\",\n            edgecolor=EDGE_COLOR,\n            hatch=ROLE_HATCHES.get(role, \"\"),\n            label=ROLE_LABELS.get(role, role),\n            linewidth=LINE_WIDTH,\n        )\n        for role in ROLE_ORDER\n        if role in summary[\"role_unified\"].unique()\n    ]\n\n    fig.legend(\n        handles=role_legend_handles,\n        loc=\"upper center\",\n        ncol=min(len(role_legend_handles), 4),\n        bbox_to_anchor=(0.5, 1.02),\n        frameon=True,\n        fontsize=LEGEND_SIZE,\n        title=\"Role pattern\",\n        title_fontsize=LEGEND_SIZE,\n    )\n\n    fig.suptitle(\n        f\"GoEmotions Stacked Bar Charts ({start + 1}-{start + len(chunk)} Opus)\",\n        fontsize=SUPTITLE_SIZE,\n        y=1.03,\n    )\n    plt.show()\n\nprint(\"=== stacked bar by emotion (emotion palette variant) done ===\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-17T19:11:55.36148Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-17T19:11:55.362085Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-17T19:12:00.837955Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-17T19:11:55.362042Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-17T19:12:00.837099Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 6. Role-centric stacked bars\nSingle-opus full-emotion view.\nA one-work-per-figure layout that shows all emotions appearing in each work.\n\nThis version is especially useful for emotion-rich sessions.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==================== CELL 7 FINAL: one opus per figure + all appeared emotions ====================\n# 目的:\n# - 1作品ずつ個別表示\n# - その作品で出現した感情をすべて表示（0は出さない）\n# - legend を上に逃がして、被りを減らす\n# - 文字サイズを少し大きくして見やすくする\n#\n# 前提:\n# - CELL 2 実行済み\n# - SUMMARY_CSV, GOEMOTIONS_LABELS, ROLE_LABELS が定義済み\n# - EMOTION_COLORS が定義済み（未定義でも fallback あり）\n\nsummary = pd.read_csv(SUMMARY_CSV)\n\nWORKS_PER_FIG = 1\nTOP_N_EMOTIONS = None          # 全出現感情を出す。上位15に戻すなら 15\nPLOT_ZERO_EMOTIONS = False     # 0感情は表示しない\nSORT_MODE = \"count\"           # \"count\" or \"label\"\nFIG_WIDTH = 24\nFIG_HEIGHT = 12.8\nROLE_TICK_SIZE = 20\nY_TICK_SIZE = 14\nTITLE_SIZE = 30\nAXIS_LABEL_SIZE = 17\nLEGEND_SIZE = 20\nSUPTITLE_SIZE = 22\nBASE_ROLE_ORDER = [\"user\", \"assistant_a\", \"assistant_b\"]\nLEGEND_NCOL = 4\nLEGEND_Y = 0.965\nTIGHT_RECT_TOP = 0.84\n\nprint(f\"WORKS_PER_FIG={WORKS_PER_FIG}\")\nprint(f\"TOP_N_EMOTIONS={TOP_N_EMOTIONS}\")\nprint(f\"PLOT_ZERO_EMOTIONS={PLOT_ZERO_EMOTIONS}\")\nprint(f\"SORT_MODE={SORT_MODE}\")\n\n\ndef prepare_role_layout_tables(summary_df, work_name):\n    sub = summary_df[summary_df[\"work\"] == work_name].copy()\n    if sub.empty:\n        return None, None, None, None\n\n    count_table = sub.pivot_table(\n        index=\"role_unified\",\n        columns=\"label\",\n        values=\"count\",\n        aggfunc=\"sum\",\n        fill_value=0,\n    )\n\n    role_order = [r for r in BASE_ROLE_ORDER if r in count_table.index]\n    if \"unknown\" in count_table.index and count_table.loc[\"unknown\"].sum() > 0:\n        role_order.append(\"unknown\")\n\n    if not role_order:\n        return None, None, None, None\n\n    count_table = count_table.loc[role_order]\n\n    if PLOT_ZERO_EMOTIONS:\n        count_table = count_table.reindex(columns=GOEMOTIONS_LABELS, fill_value=0)\n    else:\n        count_table = count_table.loc[:, count_table.sum(axis=0) > 0]\n\n    if count_table.empty:\n        return None, None, None, None\n\n    emotion_totals = count_table.sum(axis=0)\n\n    if SORT_MODE == \"label\":\n        selected_emotions = [lbl for lbl in GOEMOTIONS_LABELS if lbl in emotion_totals.index]\n    else:\n        selected_emotions = emotion_totals.sort_values(ascending=False).index.tolist()\n\n    if TOP_N_EMOTIONS is not None:\n        selected_emotions = selected_emotions[:TOP_N_EMOTIONS]\n\n    count_table = count_table[selected_emotions]\n\n    row_sums = count_table.sum(axis=1).replace(0, np.nan)\n    pct_table = count_table.div(row_sums, axis=0).fillna(0) * 100\n\n    fallback = plt.get_cmap(\"tab20\")\n    color_map = {}\n    for i, emo in enumerate(selected_emotions):\n        color_map[emo] = EMOTION_COLORS.get(emo, fallback(i % 20))\n\n    return count_table, pct_table, role_order, color_map\n\n\ndef plot_role_layout_pair(ax_pct, ax_cnt, work_name, count_table, pct_table, role_order, color_map):\n    labels = [ROLE_LABELS.get(r, r) for r in role_order]\n    x = np.arange(len(role_order))\n\n    bottom_pct = np.zeros(len(role_order))\n    bottom_cnt = np.zeros(len(role_order))\n\n    for emotion in count_table.columns:\n        pct_vals = pct_table[emotion].values\n        cnt_vals = count_table[emotion].values\n        color = color_map.get(emotion, \"#999999\")\n\n        ax_pct.bar(x, pct_vals, bottom=bottom_pct, width=0.72, color=color, label=emotion)\n        ax_cnt.bar(x, cnt_vals, bottom=bottom_cnt, width=0.72, color=color, label=emotion)\n\n        bottom_pct += pct_vals\n        bottom_cnt += cnt_vals\n\n    ax_pct.set_title(f\"{work_name} | 100% stacked by role\", fontsize=TITLE_SIZE, pad=14)\n    ax_pct.set_xticks(x)\n    ax_pct.set_xticklabels(labels, fontsize=ROLE_TICK_SIZE)\n    ax_pct.set_ylabel(\"%\", fontsize=AXIS_LABEL_SIZE)\n    ax_pct.set_ylim(0, 100)\n    ax_pct.yaxis.set_major_formatter(mtick.PercentFormatter())\n    ax_pct.grid(axis=\"y\", alpha=0.3)\n    ax_pct.tick_params(axis=\"y\", labelsize=Y_TICK_SIZE)\n\n    ax_cnt.set_title(f\"{work_name} | stacked counts by role\", fontsize=TITLE_SIZE, pad=14)\n    ax_cnt.set_xticks(x)\n    ax_cnt.set_xticklabels(labels, fontsize=ROLE_TICK_SIZE)\n    ax_cnt.set_ylabel(\"count\", fontsize=AXIS_LABEL_SIZE)\n    ax_cnt.grid(axis=\"y\", alpha=0.3)\n    ax_cnt.tick_params(axis=\"y\", labelsize=Y_TICK_SIZE)\n\n\nworks = summary[\"work\"].dropna().unique().tolist()\nprint(f\"Works: {len(works)}\")\n\nfor work_name in works:\n    count_table, pct_table, role_order, color_map = prepare_role_layout_tables(summary, work_name)\n    if count_table is None or pct_table is None:\n        print(f\"skip: {work_name}\")\n        continue\n\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(\n        nrows=1,\n        ncols=2,\n        figsize=(FIG_WIDTH, FIG_HEIGHT),\n        constrained_layout=False,\n    )\n\n    ax_pct, ax_cnt = axes[0], axes[1]\n    plot_role_layout_pair(ax_pct, ax_cnt, work_name, count_table, pct_table, role_order, color_map)\n\n    legend_handles, legend_labels = ax_pct.get_legend_handles_labels()\n    if legend_handles:\n        fig.legend(\n            legend_handles,\n            legend_labels,\n            loc=\"upper center\",\n            ncol=LEGEND_NCOL,\n            bbox_to_anchor=(0.5, LEGEND_Y),\n            frameon=True,\n            fontsize=LEGEND_SIZE,\n        )\n\n    fig.suptitle(\n        f\"GoEmotions Role-Centric Stacked Bars ({work_name})\",\n        fontsize=SUPTITLE_SIZE,\n        y=0.995,\n    )\n\n    plt.tight_layout(rect=[0, 0, 1, TIGHT_RECT_TOP])\n    plt.show()\n\nprint(\"=== CELL 7 final single-opus view done ===\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-17T21:16:14.509923Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-17T21:16:14.510599Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-17T21:16:18.705519Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-17T21:16:14.510565Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-17T21:16:18.704648Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 7. Quick tuning notes\nSmall adjustments for readability, layout, legend spacing, and figure scale.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"#nap nap nap","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-17T20:35:35.269646Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-17T20:35:35.270357Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-17T20:35:35.273611Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-17T20:35:35.270323Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-17T20:35:35.272609Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Related links\nIf you would like to explore the original Japanese creative-writing sessions,\nplease also visi